-digit\n    positive integers that start or end with 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use the principle of inclusion-exclusion: |A U B| = |A| + |B| - |A ^ B|\n    # where A is numbers starting with 1, and B is numbers ending with 1.\n\n    starts_with_1_count = _calculate_starts_with_1(n)\n    ends_with_1_count = _calculate_ends_with_1(n)\n    starts_and_ends_with_1_count = _calculate_starts_and_ends_with_1(n)\n\n    return starts_with_1_count + ends_with_1_count - starts_and_ends_with_1_count", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/139": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/139", "solution": "def special_factorial(n):\n    \"\"\"The Brazilian factorial is defined as:\n    brazilian_factorial(n) = n! * (n-1)! * (n-2)! * ... * 1!\n    where n > 0\n\n    The function will receive an integer as input and should return the special\n    factorial of this integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _factorial(k):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the standard factorial of an integer k recursively.\"\"\"\n        if k == 1:\n            return 1\n        return k * _factorial(k - 1)\n\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        result *= _factorial(i)\n    return result", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}]}}